---
title: Securing FOSSBilling
---

## Configuration Options

These settings live in your `config.php` file and control various security features.

### Security Options

| Property | Default | Options | Description |
|----------|---------|---------|-------------|
| `mode` | `strict` | `strict` or `regular` | In `strict` mode, cookies use `SameSite=Strict` and `HttpOnly`. `regular` mode uses default cookie properties but still sets `HttpOnly`. |
| `force_https` | `true` | `bool` | When enabled, FOSSBilling redirects all requests to HTTPS and forces cookies to be sent only over secure connections. |
| `session_lifespan` | `7200` | `int` | How long sessions remain valid (in seconds). Default is 2 hours. After this, sessions expire and are destroyed. |

```php
// Example configuration
'security' => [
    'mode' => 'strict',
    'force_https' => true,
    'session_lifespan' => 7200,
],
```

### API Security

| Property | Default | Options | Description |
|----------|---------|---------|-------------|
| `CSRFPrevention` | `true` | `bool` | Enables CSRF protection. Keep this enabled unless it's causing specific issues. |

```php
// Example configuration
'api' => [
    'CSRFPrevention' => true,
],
```

## Cloudflare

If you're using Cloudflare, enable **IP Geolocation** under your website's **Network** settings. This lets FOSSBilling use the visitor's country (based on IP) to help prevent session hijacking.

## Reverse Proxies

### HTTPS Detection

Reverse proxies often make FOSSBilling think it's being accessed over HTTP, even when the end user is on HTTPS. To fix this, ensure your reverse proxy forwards the `X-Forwarded-Proto` header set to `https`.

### Trusted Proxies

If you're behind a reverse proxy, you may also need to configure trusted proxy settings in FOSSBilling to ensure security features work correctly.
